 "summary": "Aru territory part 2 (Adi, Adja, Laybo and Biringi areas, northern Ituri on the Uganda and South Sudan borders) is outside the Ituri conflict core (CODECO in Djugu/Mahagi, ADF in Irumu/Mambasa). It is assessed as state-held: PNC with administration in towns such as Ingbokolo, Atsinia, Mobiri and Laybo, and FARDC deployed along the borders. The northern border strip is noted for occasional cross-border incursions but no armed-group control is known. NOTE: no web research was possible for this unit; all zones are default-presence or low-confidence inferences.",
